<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $59 mln Feb 6.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $59 mln Feb 6.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $59-million deficit on Feb 6 in the commercial forex market, according to central bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON FEBRUARY 6</p>
<p>Exports: $172.2 million</p>
<p>Imports: $213.6 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $189.1 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $206.7 million</p>
<p>Deficit: $59 million</p>
<p>FEBRUARY DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $763.6 million</p>
<p>Imports: $622.3 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $831.7 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $767.6 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $205.4 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 248-5418))</p>
